---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
import '../styles/legal.css';
---

<Layout
	title="Terms of Use"
	description="Rules for using VideoVault and its Monthly, Yearly, and Lifetime Pro plans."
	canonicalPath="/terms/"
>
	<article class="legal container">
		<nav class="legal__nav" aria-label="Legal">
			<a href="/">Home</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.privacy}>Privacy Policy</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.terms} aria-current="page">Terms of Use</a>
			<a href={siteConfig.legal.support}>Support</a>
		</nav>

		<h1>VideoVault Terms of Use</h1>
		<p class="legal__meta">
			<strong>Effective date:</strong> July 16, 2026<br />
			<strong>Last updated:</strong> October 12, 2026
		</p>

		<h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
		<p>
			By downloading or using VideoVault: Media Player, you agree to these Terms of Use. If you do
			not agree, do not use the app.
		</p>

		<h2>2. What VideoVault does</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault is a media utility for playing and importing supported media, organizing Private
			Lists, using Web Import with compatible sources, background playback, Picture in Picture,
			AirPlay, Video Studio, Audio Tools, exporting, sharing, and backing up or restoring a library.
		</p>

		<h2>3. License</h2>
		<p>
			Subject to these terms and applicable App Store rules, you receive a limited, personal,
			non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable license to use VideoVault on Apple devices you own or
			control.
		</p>

		<h2>4. Your media and legal responsibility</h2>
		<p>
			You retain ownership of media you import or create. You are responsible for having the rights
			and permissions required to use, edit, export, share, or distribute that media.
		</p>
		<p>
			You must not use VideoVault to infringe copyright, privacy, publicity, or other rights;
			distribute unlawful content; bypass digital rights management; or violate applicable law.
		</p>

		<h2>5. Pro plans and purchases</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault Pro is offered as Monthly and Yearly auto-renewing subscriptions and as a one-time,
			non-consumable Lifetime purchase through Apple’s App Store.
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Monthly is currently $0.99/month and Yearly is $9.99/year in the US storefront. Lifetime Pro is a $19.99 one-time purchase; Apple shows its current price before purchase.</li>
			<li>Eligible new Monthly subscribers may receive a 7-day free trial. Eligibility is determined by Apple and confirmed before purchase.</li>
			<li>Subscriptions renew automatically unless canceled through Apple account settings at least 24 hours before the end of the current period, subject to Apple’s applicable terms.</li>
			<li>
				Payment, billing, refunds, transaction history, and purchase authorization are handled by
				Apple.
			</li>
			<li>
				Restore Purchase restores an eligible App Store entitlement; it does not restore media files
				or Private Lists.
			</li>
			<li>Full Library Backup and Restore are separate from purchase restoration.</li>
			<li>
				Prices and tax treatment may vary by storefront and are shown by Apple before purchase.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>6. Local storage, backup, and data loss</h2>
		<p>
			VideoVault primarily stores media and Private Lists locally in the app container. Deleting the app
			can remove those local files. Before deleting VideoVault, resetting a device, or changing
			devices, save a Full Library Backup to iCloud Drive or another external location and verify that
			the backup file exists.
		</p>
		<p>
			We cannot recover media or backups that were never exported and are no longer present on your
			device or storage provider. Nothing in these terms excludes rights or remedies that cannot
			legally be excluded.
		</p>

		<h2>7. Availability and compatibility</h2>
		<p>
			Features may depend on device hardware, operating system support, available storage,
			permissions, network access, Apple services, and third-party file providers. Picture in
			Picture, background behavior, sharing destinations, and file-provider features may vary by
			device and system version.
		</p>

		<h2>8. Prohibited conduct</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>
				Reverse engineering, tampering, or attempting to bypass purchase verification except where
				applicable law expressly permits it.
			</li>
			<li>Using the app to harm devices, services, or other people.</li>
			<li>Misrepresenting ownership or authorization for media.</li>
			<li>Using VideoVault in violation of App Store rules or applicable law.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2>9. Updates and changes</h2>
		<p>
			We may update VideoVault to fix bugs, improve security, add or remove features, or maintain
			compatibility. Some updates may require a newer version of iOS or iPadOS.
		</p>

		<h2>10. Disclaimer</h2>
		<p>
			To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, VideoVault is provided “as is” and “as
			available.” We do not guarantee uninterrupted operation, compatibility with every media file or
			provider, or recovery of data that was not successfully backed up.
		</p>

		<h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
		<p>
			To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect, incidental,
			special, or consequential loss arising from use of the app, including loss caused by app
			deletion, device failure, insufficient storage, damaged files, or unavailable third-party
			services. This limitation does not apply where prohibited by law.
		</p>

		<h2>12. Apple</h2>
		<p>
			Apple is not responsible for providing maintenance or support for VideoVault except as required
			by applicable App Store terms. Apple and its subsidiaries may be third-party beneficiaries of
			the applicable end-user license terms.
		</p>

		<h2>13. Termination</h2>
		<p>
			Your right to use VideoVault ends if you materially violate these terms. Sections that by their
			nature should survive termination will continue to apply.
		</p>

		<h2>14. Contact</h2>
		<p>
			Questions about these terms:{' '}
			<a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a>
		</p>
	</article>
</Layout>
